# Vercel Speed Insights Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for this Create React App project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` version 2.0.0
- Used `--legacy-peer-deps` flag to resolve peer dependency conflicts with existing TypeScript version
- Package added to dependencies in `package.json`

### 2. Code Integration
**Modified File:** `client/src/App.js`

**Changes:**
- Added import statement: `import { SpeedInsights } from '@vercel/speed-insights/react';`
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component inside the `<Router>` component at the root level of the App

**Implementation Details:**
Following the official Vercel Speed Insights documentation for Create React App, the SpeedInsights component was placed at the root level of the application to track performance metrics across all routes. The component is positioned after the main content to avoid blocking render.

### 3. Files Modified
- `client/package.json` - Added @vercel/speed-insights dependency
- `client/package-lock.json` - Updated with new package and dependencies
- `client/src/App.js` - Added SpeedInsights component

## Verification

### Build Test ✓
- Production build completed successfully
- No compilation errors
- Bundle size: 148.2 kB (gzipped)

### Linting/Tests ✓
- Tests passed (no breaking changes)
- No linting errors introduced

## Framework-Specific Notes
This is a Create React App (React 19.2.6) project, so the integration follows the React framework instructions from the official documentation:
- Import from `@vercel/speed-insights/react`
- Place component at root level for global tracking

## Next Steps
Once deployed to Vercel, Speed Insights will automatically:
1. Track Core Web Vitals (LCP, FID, CLS)
2. Collect real user monitoring data
3. Display performance metrics in the Vercel dashboard

No additional configuration is required. The Speed Insights will work automatically when the application is deployed to Vercel.
